    "body": "Coordinator: a decision on the block rule, from the first run of the worker.\n\nThe first form of the rule blocked the post when the cut is deeper than the flute and the shank is wider than the cutter. The quick gate showed that this is wrong: the test `t31_verify_judges_shank_at_6_35_below_38_1_and_catches_real_holder_hit` has a 2D Contour with a flute of 14.478 mm, a cut of 25 mm and a wider shank, and the verifier finds no collision there (the shank goes beside the wall, not in it). A wider shank below the flute is thus not a certain collision. With the block, a program that posted before did not post.\n\nMaintainer decision (owner's standing word 2026-11-22: choose the recommended option while he sleeps). Options: (1) `FluteShort` is always advisory and is listed first; the existing shank and holder findings hold the post when the body does meet material; (2) keep the block for a wider shank and accept that the program of `t31` does not post; (3) block only when a shank finding exists also (the same result as (1), with more code). Taken: **(1)**. Reason: the diagnostic exists to name the cause; the collision checks decide if the post is held. The case of #3319 stays blocked by its shank findings, and it now names the cause first.\n\nThe worker changes the rule, the decision file and the three tests that assert an exact list of findings or notes (they get the new first finding or the new note; no finding is removed).\n",
